'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-vo-s037-cogatn-self.spin2
''   Purpose....  VO-S037: does COGATN with the issuing cog's own bit set
''                (COGATN(1 << COGID())) raise an attention event in that
''                same cog?  PASM POLLATN / JATN / WAITATN and Spin2 POLLATN()
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-S037; close-out study step 8)

  The sources do not say whether a cog can strobe itself:
    - silicon-doc-text.txt:2020: "The 16 attention strobe outputs from all
      cogs are OR'd together to form a composite set of 16 strobes, from
      which each cog receives its particular strobe" - does not exclude the
      issuing cog;
    - SD:2053: "Event 14 = Attention was requested by another cog or other
      cogs" - reads the other way;
    - SD:2203: the POLLATN/WAITATN flag is "Set whenever any cogs request
      attention", "Cleared on cog start", "Also cleared on POLLATN/WAITATN/
      JATN/JNATN" (SD:2200-2204);
    - spin2-v55-text.txt:526-528: COGATN(CogMask) "Strobe ATN input(s) of
      cog(s) according to 16-bit CogMask"; POLLATN() "Check if this cog has
      received an ATN strobe, AtnFlag = -1 if ATN strobed or 0 if not
      strobed"; WAITATN() "Wait for this cog to receive an ATN strobe".
  The KB page methods/cogatn.yaml says "Cannot signal yourself (no effect)":
  unsourced.  The page's claim is deleted regardless of this bench (the
  delete-the-claim fix needs no measurement); the bench only decides whether
  the OPPOSITE may be stated.

  THIS PROGRAM MEASURES AND PREDICTS NOTHING.  A target cog strobes ITSELF
  and looks for the event, in four forms, each with a control and a negative
  control on the very same cog, repetition by repetition:
    F0  PASM POLLATN WC in a poll loop bounded by a window
    F1  PASM JATN #hit in a loop bounded by a window
    F2  PASM SETQ <CT target> + WAITATN WC (SD:2084: SETQ before WAITxxx gives
        a CT timeout; "C will be set if the timeout occurred before the
        event"); the wait is bounded by the CT target, so it cannot hang
    F3  Spin2  COGATN(1 << COGID()) then a POLLATN() loop bounded by the
        same window (a Spin2 WAITATN() has no timeout and is NOT used).  In
        the Spin2 interpreter COGATN(mask) is the instruction "cogatn x"
        (Spin2_interpreter.spin2:1109, bytecode $2E at :930) and POLLATN() is
        "pollatn wc" (:1125 'waitatn_ pollatn wc'; bytecode $2F at :931), so F3 reaches the
        same silicon instruction as F0 by the Spin2 route
  For each form and repetition three CELLS run, in this order, with the
  target's attention flag cleared first (two POLLATN/POLLATN() before the
  cell; the second MUST read 0):
    CTRL  a SECOND cog (the helper) strobes the target (documented use).
          Must be delivered 8 of 8 or the rig is void.
    SELF  the target strobes itself: the question.
    NEG   nothing strobes: the window must read "no event" 8 of 8 or the
          rig is void (a detector that fires with no strobe proves nothing).
  The CTRL cell runs immediately before the SELF cell in every repetition:
  it is the marker that the poll/jump/wait path of that form is alive in
  THIS repetition.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  NO PINS, no jumper, nothing attached.
  Cog 0 (Spin2, the only cog with the debugger, DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001)
  starts, in this order:
    H  the helper (PASM): waits for a request (id, mask) in the mailbox,
       executes COGATN <mask>, then writes the id to the ack long; it stops
       on a stop flag or after 3 s;
    T  the PASM target: runs forms F0, F1, F2 (8 repetitions x 3 cells each);
    U  the Spin2 target (cogspin): runs form F3.
  T and U run one after the other (never together); H serves both.  Cog 0
  waits for each with a 1 s timeout, stops H, T and U if still running, and
  reports.  Nothing runs concurrently with a measurement except H.
  The interaction is STRUCTURAL, not timed: the target posts a request and
  WAITS (bounded: 2 ms) for H's ack before opening the observation window; the
  ack is written by H only AFTER its COGATN has executed.  The window is 100 us
  (20,000 clocks), 10,000x longer than the 2-clock COGATN; an event that
  arrives is polled until it is seen, never sampled once.  If H never
  answers, the ack times out and the cell is flagged (RIG FAIL).

THE CELL (PASM, target T)
    pre-clear   POLLATN WC / WRC p1 / POLLATN WC / WRC p2   (p2 MUST be 0;
                p1 is the residue of the previous cell and MUST be 0 too:
                a late event from an earlier cell would show here)
    stimulus    CTRL: write mask (1 << T's COGID), write the request id,
                      wait for the ack     SELF: COGATN (1 << COGID)
                NEG: none
    window      form F0/F1: loop until the event or 20,000 clocks (GETCT)
                form F2: SETQ (GETCT + 20,000) / WAITATN WC; C = timeout
    record      4 longs: tag, delivered (1/0), clocks from the window's
                start to the event (or 20,000), pre-flags (bit 0 p1, bit 1
                p2, bit 2 = ack received, 1 when there was no request)
  The tag is written in the same block; a cell never written shows a wrong
  tag.

PRE-REGISTERED READINGS OF THE SELF CELLS (printed BEFORE the run)
    DELIVERED      SELF delivered in 8 of 8 repetitions, as CTRL: a cog can
                   strobe itself
    NOT DELIVERED  SELF delivered in 0 of 8, as NEG: a self strobe is lost
    MIXED          anything else: reported as the finding, never a pass
  One reading per form.  If the forms disagree that is printed as the finding.

CHECKS (each failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT)
    - H, T and U started, and T and U finished within 1 s;
    - every cell has its tag;
    - every cell's pre-clear read 0 twice (no residue);
    - every CTRL cell got the helper's ack in time (SELF and NEG make no
      request, so their ack flag is set by definition);
    - CTRL delivered 8 of 8 in every form; NEG delivered 0 of 8 in every form.

DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF
  The brief's arms (i)-(iv) are run per FORM and per repetition (8
  repetitions, 4 forms) so a control and a negative control sit next to each
  SELF cell.  The brief's "WAITATN with a timeout" is the SETQ form (F2),
  because a plain WAITATN could hang the cog.  The brief's "JATN repeat" is
  F1.  A Spin2 WAITATN() form is deliberately absent (no timeout).

DEBUGGER
  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub strings and numbers and
  sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in ln_out(); the only other
  record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").

OPCODES AND ADDRESSES  (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8, read from the .lst)
  The .lst is a hub-image dump plus a symbol table.  Two PASM cogs, each
  assembled at cog address 0: the helper at object offset $54 (+ cog address
  * 4), the target at $B4 (+ cog address * 4).  Encodings from the silicon
  doc: COGATN D/# = EEEE 1101011 00L DDDDDDDDD 000111111 (silicon-doc-text.txt
  :5351), POLLATN {WCZ} = EEEE 1101011 CZ0 000001110 000100100 (:5283),
  WAITATN = ... 000011110 000100100 (:5300), JATN S/# = EEEE 1011110 01I
  000001110 SSSSSSSSS (:5181).  Read from the .lst:
    helper $070  cogatn h_mask        $FD60_2C3F   (D = h_mask $16, L = 0)
    helper $074  wrlong h_id,ptra[2]  $FC64_2B02   (the ack, AFTER the cogatn)
    helper $078  rdlong h_stop,ptra[3] $FB04_2F03
    target $0F0  pollatn wc           $FD70_1C24   (pre-clear 1; again at $0F8)
    target $140  cmp c_kind,#K_SELF wz $F20C_D801, then
    target $144  if_z cogatn c_selfmask $AD60_D03F (D = c_selfmask $68; the
                                                    question; conditional on SELF)
    target $164  setq c_dl            $FD60_EA28   (D = c_dl $75)
    target $168  waitatn wc           $FD70_3C24   (the very next long)
    target $174  pollatn wc           $FD70_1C24   (F0 loop; w_poll)
    target $190  jatn #w_hit          $FBCC_1C05   (F1 loop; w_jatn; rel9 +5)
    target $204  setq #3              $FD64_0628   (RECW - 1) then
    target $208  wrlong g_tag,c_idx   $FC60_EC6F   (the 4-long record)
  Cog registers, target: c_window $62, c_ackbud $63, c_tagbase $64, c_donev
  $65, c_recbase $66, c_me $67, c_selfmask $68, c_rid $69, c_rep $6A, c_form
  $6B, c_kind $6C, c_prog $6D, c_tmp $6E, c_idx $6F, c_p1 $70, c_p2 $71,
  c_ack $72, c_t0 $73, c_t1 $74, c_dl $75, record block g_tag $76, g_del $77,
  g_lat $78, g_pre $79 (contiguous).  Helper: h_budget $11 .. h_stop $17.
  Mailbox longs: MB_REQID 0, MB_MASK 1, MB_ACK 2, MB_STOP 3, MB_TREC 4,
  MB_TCUR 5, MB_TDONE 6.
  The listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.
  If you edit this file, recompile with -l and re-read every row above.

HOW TO RUN
  USB serial must be connected (DEBUG rides P62/P63).  Compile with
  pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10).
  Runs once, in well under a second; nothing is written to flash.
  SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT - it is the only record.
  Expected run time: well under 1 s; at most about 2 s (each target is waited
  for at most 1 s).  A run that prints no "=== END" line and no
  DEBUG_END_SESSION within 10 s is a hang or a lost session: report it as
  such, not as a reading.
  Clock: _clkfreq = 200 MHz assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal (the listing's
  CLKMODE is $010009FB, read from the .lst); the window (20,000 clocks), the
  2 ms ack budget and the 1 s waits depend on it.
  A STALLED target (progress long printed) voids its forms: their per-cell
  lines are not printed and no VERDICT is given.
  Output: the header and pre-registered readings, one line per form, the
  VERDICT lines, the END line, then DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000         ' system clock: 200 MHz
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  REPS            = 8                   ' repetitions of every cell
  NFORM           = 4                   ' F0 POLLATN, F1 JATN, F2 WAITATN+SETQ, F3 Spin2
  NPFORM          = 3                   ' forms run by the PASM target
  NKIND           = 3                   ' CTRL, SELF, NEG
  RECW            = 4                   ' longs per cell record
  WINDOW          = 20_000              ' clocks of observation window (100 us)
  ACK_BUDGET      = 400_000             ' clocks to wait for the helper's ack (2 ms)
  HELPER_BUDGET   = 600_000_000         ' the helper stops by itself after 3 s
  TAG_BASE        = $5037_0000          ' cell tag = TAG_BASE + form * 256 + kind * 16 + rep
  RID_T           = $0100               ' request ids of the PASM target
  RID_U           = $0200               ' request ids of the Spin2 target
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E          ' a cog is done
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' fill before a run

  SPIN_STACK      = 64
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars)
  DEC_TOP         = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS      = 10
  DEC_BASE        = 10
  HEX_DIGITS      = 8
  HEX_BITS        = 4
  HEX_GROUP       = 4
  HEX_LETTERS     = 10

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' forms
  #0, F_POLL, F_JATN, F_WAIT, F_SPIN
  ' cell kinds (the order they run in, inside a repetition)
  #0, K_CTRL, K_SELF, K_NEG
  ' cell record longs
  #0, C_TAG, C_DEL, C_LAT, C_PRE
  ' pre-flag bits
  PRE_P1          = %001                ' residue read by the first pre-clear POLLATN
  PRE_P2          = %010                ' residue read by the second pre-clear POLLATN
  PRE_ACK         = %100                ' the helper's ack arrived (set when no request was made)
  ' mailbox longs (cog 0, helper, targets)
  '  MB_REQID  - request id (written last)   MB_MASK - attention mask
  '  MB_ACK    - last id acknowledged by the helper (written after COGATN)
  '  MB_STOP   - non-zero: the helper stops  MB_TREC - hub address of T's records
  '  MB_TCUR   - T's progress: form * 256 + kind * 16 + rep
  '  MB_TDONE  - DONE_V when T is done
  #0, MB_REQID, MB_MASK, MB_ACK, MB_STOP, MB_TREC, MB_TCUR, MB_TDONE, MB_LEN

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  long tRecs[NPFORM * NKIND * REPS * RECW]  ' [form][kind][rep][field], PASM target
  long uRecs[NKIND * REPS * RECW]           ' [kind][rep][field], Spin2 target
  long uCur                             ' U progress: kind * 16 + rep
  long uDone                            ' DONE_V when U is done
  long spinStack[SPIN_STACK]
  long failCnt                          ' RIG FAIL lines printed
  long bTStall, bUStall
  long cogH, cogT, cogU
  long uMask                            ' U's own mask (for the report)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | formIdx
'' Start the helper, the PASM target and the Spin2 target one after the other,
'' check the controls, report every form.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local formIdx - form

  linePos := 0
  failCnt := 0
  bTStall := FALSE
  bUStall := FALSE
  print_header()

  longfill(@tRecs, UNWRITTEN, NPFORM * NKIND * REPS * RECW)
  longfill(@uRecs, UNWRITTEN, NKIND * REPS * RECW)
  longfill(@mbox, 0, MB_LEN)
  mbox[MB_TREC] := @tRecs
  mbox[MB_TCUR] := UNWRITTEN
  uCur := UNWRITTEN
  uDone := 0

  cogH := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @helper, @mbox)
  if cogH < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog for the helper, got "))
    ln_d(cogH)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no helper cog) - NO VERDICT ==="))
    finish()

  cogT := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @target, @mbox)
  if cogT < 0
    cogstop(cogH)
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog for the PASM target, got "))
    ln_d(cogT)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no PASM target cog) - NO VERDICT ==="))
    finish()
  if not wait_done(@mbox[MB_TDONE])
    bTStall := TRUE
    cogstop(cogT)

  cogU := cogspin(NEWCOG, spin_target(), @spinStack)
  if cogU < 0
    cogstop(cogH)
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: cogspin expected a free cog for the Spin2 target, got "))
    ln_d(cogU)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no Spin2 target cog) - NO VERDICT ==="))
    finish()
  if not wait_done(@uDone)
    bUStall := TRUE
    cogstop(cogU)

  mbox[MB_STOP] := 1
  cogstop(cogH)

  ln_s(string("=== helper cog "))
  ln_d(cogH)
  ln_s(string(", PASM target cog "))
  ln_d(cogT)
  ln_s(string(" (mask "))
  ln_h(1 << cogT)
  ln_s(string("), Spin2 target cog "))
  ln_d(cogU)
  ln_s(string(" (mask "))
  ln_h(uMask)
  say(string(") ==="))
  if bTStall
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: STALLED - the PASM target did not finish within 1 s; progress long "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_TCUR])
    ln_s(string(" (form * 256 + kind * 16 + rep, UNWRITTEN = never started)"))
    ln_out()
    failCnt++
  if bUStall
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: STALLED - the Spin2 target did not finish within 1 s; progress long "))
    ln_h(uCur)
    ln_s(string(" (kind * 16 + rep, UNWRITTEN = never started)"))
    ln_out()
    failCnt++
  if bTStall or bUStall
    say(string("RIG FAIL above: the per-cell lines of a STALLED target are NOT printed (its cells are unwritten, any reading would be noise - ignore); a target that finished is still reported"))

  repeat formIdx from F_POLL to F_SPIN
    if (formIdx == F_SPIN and bUStall) or (formIdx <> F_SPIN and bTStall)
      ln_s(form_text(formIdx))
      say(string(": not reported - its target stalled (see RIG FAIL above)"))
    else
      report_form(formIdx)
  print_verdict()
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output.
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_d(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as signed

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_cnt(countVal)
' Append "n of 8".
'
' @param countVal - the count

  ln_d(countVal)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(REPS)

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI rig_fail(pStr)
' Count one RIG FAIL and start its line; the caller appends the details and
' sends the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the text

  failCnt++
  ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
  ln_s(pStr)

PRI wait_done(pFlag) : bDone | startCt
' Wait up to 1 s for a cog to write DONE_V to its done long.
'
' @param pFlag - hub address of the done long
' @returns bDone - TRUE when DONE_V arrived in time

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the wait began

  bDone := TRUE
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until long[pFlag] == DONE_V
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      bDone := FALSE
      quit

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' header
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header()
' Print the rig identity and the pre-registered readings, before any run.
'

  say(string("=== VO-S037: does COGATN(1 << COGID()) strobe the issuing cog? (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz, no pins) ==="))
  say(string("Measured, not predicted: SD:2020 does not exclude the issuing cog, SD:2053 says 'another cog'; no source states it. Forms: F0 PASM POLLATN | F1 PASM JATN | F2 PASM SETQ+WAITATN WC | F3 Spin2 POLLATN()."))
  say(string("Per form and repetition, three cells, flag cleared first (2 polls, the 2nd MUST read 0): CTRL = a helper cog strobes the target | SELF = the target strobes itself | NEG = no strobe. Window 20,000 clocks, polled to the end."))
  say(string("Gates (else RIG FAIL, NO VERDICT): CTRL delivered 8 of 8 and NEG delivered 0 of 8 in every form; every pre-clear reads 0; every ack arrives; every cell has its tag."))
  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED READINGS of the SELF cells (one per form; none predicted):"))
  say(string("  DELIVERED     = SELF delivered 8 of 8, as CTRL: a cog can strobe itself"))
  say(string("  NOT DELIVERED = SELF delivered 0 of 8, as NEG: a self strobe is lost"))
  say(string("  MIXED         = anything else: the finding, never a pass"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' records
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : fieldVal
' One field of one cell.
'
' @param formIdx - F_POLL .. F_SPIN
' @param kindIdx - K_CTRL, K_SELF, K_NEG
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - C_TAG .. C_PRE
' @returns fieldVal - the recorded long

  if formIdx == F_SPIN
    fieldVal := uRecs[(kindIdx * REPS + repIdx) * RECW + fieldIdx]
  else
    fieldVal := tRecs[((formIdx * NKIND + kindIdx) * REPS + repIdx) * RECW + fieldIdx]

PRI form_text(formIdx) : pText
' @param formIdx - form
' @returns pText - the form as printed

  pText := lookupz(formIdx: string("F0 PASM POLLATN WC    "), string("F1 PASM JATN #hit     "), string("F2 PASM SETQ+WAITATN WC"), string("F3 Spin2 COGATN+POLLATN()"))

PRI kind_text(kindIdx) : pText
' @param kindIdx - cell kind
' @returns pText - the kind as printed

  pText := lookupz(kindIdx: string("CTRL helper->target"), string("SELF target->target"), string("NEG  no strobe     "))

PRI delivered_cnt(formIdx, kindIdx) : delCnt | repIdx
' How many repetitions of a cell kind delivered the event.
'
' @param formIdx - form
' @param kindIdx - cell kind
' @returns delCnt - repetitions with delivered = 1

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition

  delCnt := 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    if cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_DEL) == 1
      delCnt++

PRI report_form(formIdx) | kindIdx, repIdx, tagCnt, preCnt, ackCnt, delCnt, latLo, latHi, latVal, tagWant
' Check one form's 24 cells, print its lines and count the RIG FAILs.
'
' @param formIdx - form

' Local Variables:
' @local kindIdx - cell kind
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local tagCnt - cells whose tag is right
' @local preCnt - cells whose two pre-clear polls read 0
' @local ackCnt - cells whose ack arrived
' @local delCnt - repetitions that delivered the event
' @local latLo - fewest clocks to the event over delivered cells
' @local latHi - most clocks to the event over delivered cells
' @local latVal - one cell's clocks
' @local tagWant - the tag a cell must carry

  repeat kindIdx from K_CTRL to K_NEG
    tagCnt := 0
    preCnt := 0
    ackCnt := 0
    latLo := POSX
    latHi := NEGX
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      tagWant := TAG_BASE + (formIdx << 8) + (kindIdx << 4) + repIdx
      if cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_TAG) == tagWant
        tagCnt++
      if (cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_PRE) & (PRE_P1 | PRE_P2)) == 0
        preCnt++
      if (cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_PRE) & PRE_ACK) <> 0
        ackCnt++
      if cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_DEL) == 1
        latVal := cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_LAT)
        latLo <#= latVal
        latHi #>= latVal
    delCnt := delivered_cnt(formIdx, kindIdx)
    ln_s(form_text(formIdx))
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(kind_text(kindIdx))
    ln_s(string(": event delivered "))
    ln_cnt(delCnt)
    if delCnt <> 0
      ln_s(string(" | clocks to the event "))
      ln_d(latLo)
      ln_s(string(".."))
      ln_d(latHi)
    ln_s(string(" | clean pre-clear "))
    ln_cnt(preCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | ack "))
    ln_cnt(ackCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | tags "))
    ln_cnt(tagCnt)
    ln_out()
    ln_s(string("   raw delivered per rep (1 = event, clocks):"))
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      ln_s(string(" | "))
      ln_d(cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_DEL))
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_d(cell_at(formIdx, kindIdx, repIdx, C_LAT))
    ln_out()
    if tagCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(form_text(formIdx))
      ln_s(string(" "))
      ln_s(kind_text(kindIdx))
      ln_s(string(" cells with the right tag "))
      ln_cnt(tagCnt)
      ln_out()
    if preCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(form_text(formIdx))
      ln_s(string(" "))
      ln_s(kind_text(kindIdx))
      ln_s(string(" pre-clear read an event in "))
      ln_d(REPS - preCnt)
      ln_s(string(" cell(s) - the attention flag was not clear before the cell"))
      ln_out()
    if kindIdx == K_CTRL and ackCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(form_text(formIdx))
      ln_s(string(" CTRL helper ack arrived in "))
      ln_cnt(ackCnt)
      ln_s(string(" - the helper cog did not strobe/answer"))
      ln_out()
    if kindIdx == K_CTRL and delCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(form_text(formIdx))
      ln_s(string(" CTRL (documented use) delivered "))
      ln_cnt(delCnt)
      ln_s(string(" (MUST be 8 of 8: the form cannot see a strobe)"))
      ln_out()
    if kindIdx == K_NEG and delCnt <> 0
      rig_fail(form_text(formIdx))
      ln_s(string(" NEG (no strobe) delivered "))
      ln_cnt(delCnt)
      ln_s(string(" (MUST be 0 of 8: a stray event)"))
      ln_out()

PRI print_verdict() | formIdx, selfCnt, nDel, nNot, nMixed
' Print one reading per form when no gate failed.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local formIdx - form
' @local selfCnt - SELF repetitions that delivered
' @local nDel - forms that read DELIVERED
' @local nNot - forms that read NOT DELIVERED
' @local nMixed - forms that read MIXED

  ln_s(string("=== CONTROLS: "))
  if failCnt == 0
    say(string("all passed ==="))
  else
    ln_d(failCnt)
    say(string(" RIG FAIL line(s) above ==="))
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a control failed, the SELF cells are not interpretable"))
    return
  nDel := 0
  nNot := 0
  nMixed := 0
  repeat formIdx from F_POLL to F_SPIN
    selfCnt := delivered_cnt(formIdx, K_SELF)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT "))
    ln_s(form_text(formIdx))
    if selfCnt == REPS
      nDel++
      say(string(": DELIVERED - the issuing cog received its own attention strobe (SELF 8 of 8, as CTRL)"))
    elseif selfCnt == 0
      nNot++
      say(string(": NOT DELIVERED - a cog's own strobe did not reach it (SELF 0 of 8, as NEG)"))
    else
      nMixed++
      say(string(": MIXED - SELF delivered in some repetitions only; INCONCLUSIVE, not a pass"))
  if nMixed == 0 and nDel == NFORM
    say(string("SUMMARY: all four forms DELIVERED - COGATN of the issuing cog's own bit raises that cog's attention event"))
  elseif nMixed == 0 and nNot == NFORM
    say(string("SUMMARY: all four forms NOT DELIVERED - a cog cannot strobe itself"))
  else
    say(string("SUMMARY: the forms do not agree, or a form is MIXED - the per-form lines above are the finding"))
  say(string("=== END ==="))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the Spin2 target (form F3)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI spin_target() | repIdx, kindIdx, rid, tStart, bAck, bFound, pre, lat, base
' Spin2 target: for every repetition run the CTRL, SELF and NEG cells with
' POLLATN() bounded by the window; write DONE_V at the end.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local kindIdx - cell kind
' @local rid - request id counter
' @local tStart - CT at the start of a wait or window
' @local bAck - the helper's ack arrived (TRUE when no request was made)
' @local bFound - the event was seen
' @local pre - pre-flags
' @local lat - clocks to the event
' @local base - index into uRecs of the cell

  uMask := 1 << cogid()
  rid := RID_U
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    repeat kindIdx from K_CTRL to K_NEG
      uCur := (kindIdx << 4) + repIdx
      pre := 0
      if pollatn() <> 0
        pre |= PRE_P1
      if pollatn() <> 0
        pre |= PRE_P2
      bAck := TRUE
      if kindIdx == K_CTRL
        rid++
        mbox[MB_MASK] := uMask
        mbox[MB_REQID] := rid
        tStart := getct()
        repeat until mbox[MB_ACK] == rid
          if getct() - tStart > ACK_BUDGET
            bAck := FALSE
            quit
      elseif kindIdx == K_SELF
        cogatn(1 << cogid())
      tStart := getct()
      bFound := FALSE
      lat := WINDOW
      repeat while getct() - tStart < WINDOW
        if pollatn() <> 0
          lat := getct() - tStart
          bFound := TRUE
          quit
      if bAck
        pre |= PRE_ACK
      base := (kindIdx * REPS + repIdx) * RECW
      uRecs[base + C_DEL] := bFound & 1
      uRecs[base + C_LAT] := lat
      uRecs[base + C_PRE] := pre
      uRecs[base + C_TAG] := TAG_BASE + (F_SPIN << 8) + (kindIdx << 4) + repIdx
  uDone := DONE_V

' ===========================================================================
' HELPER COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox.  Waits for a request id
' it has not seen, reads the mask, executes COGATN <mask>, THEN writes the id
' to the ack long.  Stops on MB_STOP or after HELPER_BUDGET clocks.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Helper Cog ----
helper          getct   h_t0
                mov     h_seen, #0
h_lp            rdlong  h_id, ptra[MB_REQID]
                cmp     h_id, h_seen                    wz
        if_z    jmp     #h_chk                          ' nothing new
                rdlong  h_mask, ptra[MB_MASK]           ' the mask was written BEFORE the id
                mov     h_seen, h_id
                cogatn  h_mask                          ' strobe the requested cog(s)
                wrlong  h_id, ptra[MB_ACK]              ' acknowledge AFTER the strobe
h_chk           rdlong  h_stop, ptra[MB_STOP]
                tjnz    h_stop, #h_end
                getct   h_t1
                sub     h_t1, h_t0
                cmp     h_t1, h_budget                  wc
        if_c    jmp     #h_lp
h_end           cogid   h_t1
                cogstop h_t1

h_budget        long    HELPER_BUDGET
h_t0            long    0
h_t1            long    0
h_seen          long    0
h_id            long    0
h_mask          long    0
h_stop          long    0
helper_end

' ===========================================================================
' PASM TARGET COG (cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox.  No debug(), no BRK, no
' interrupt.  Runs forms F0..F2: for each repetition, form, kind: one cell.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- PASM Target Cog ----
target          rdlong  c_recbase, ptra[MB_TREC]        ' hub address of the cell records
                cogid   c_me
                mov     c_selfmask, #1
                shl     c_selfmask, c_me                ' 1 << COGID
                mov     c_rid, #RID_T
                mov     c_rep, #0

rep_lp          mov     c_form, #0
form_lp         mov     c_kind, #0
kind_lp         ' ---- one cell ----
                mov     c_prog, c_form                  ' progress: form * 256 + kind * 16 + rep
                shl     c_prog, #8
                mov     c_tmp, c_kind
                shl     c_tmp, #4
                add     c_prog, c_tmp
                add     c_prog, c_rep
                wrlong  c_prog, ptra[MB_TCUR]
                ' pre-clear: two polls; both MUST read 0
                pollatn                                 wc
                wrc     c_p1
                pollatn                                 wc
                wrc     c_p2
                mov     c_ack, #1                       ' 1 = no request made, or acknowledged
                cmp     c_kind, #K_CTRL                 wz
        if_nz   jmp     #t_notctrl
                ' CTRL: ask the helper cog to strobe me, wait (bounded) for its ack
                add     c_rid, #1
                wrlong  c_selfmask, ptra[MB_MASK]
                wrlong  c_rid, ptra[MB_REQID]           ' the id is written LAST
                getct   c_t0
t_ackw          rdlong  c_tmp, ptra[MB_ACK]
                cmp     c_tmp, c_rid                    wz
        if_z    jmp     #t_window
                getct   c_t1
                sub     c_t1, c_t0
                cmp     c_t1, c_ackbud                  wc
        if_c    jmp     #t_ackw
                mov     c_ack, #0                       ' no ack in time
                jmp     #t_window
t_notctrl       cmp     c_kind, #K_SELF                 wz
        if_z    cogatn  c_selfmask                      ' THE QUESTION: strobe my own bit
                ' (NEG: no stimulus)
t_window        getct   c_t0                            ' the window starts here
                cmp     c_form, #F_POLL                 wz
        if_z    jmp     #w_poll
                cmp     c_form, #F_JATN                 wz
        if_z    jmp     #w_jatn
                ' F2: SETQ <CT target> + WAITATN WC; C = the timeout fired first
                mov     c_dl, c_t0
                add     c_dl, c_window
                setq    c_dl
                waitatn                                 wc
        if_c    jmp     #w_miss
                jmp     #w_hit
w_poll          pollatn                                 wc
        if_c    jmp     #w_hit
                getct   c_t1
                sub     c_t1, c_t0
                cmp     c_t1, c_window                  wc
        if_c    jmp     #w_poll
                jmp     #w_miss
w_jatn          jatn    #w_hit                          ' jumps (and clears the flag) on an event
                getct   c_t1
                sub     c_t1, c_t0
                cmp     c_t1, c_window                  wc
        if_c    jmp     #w_jatn
                jmp     #w_miss
w_hit           getct   c_t1
                sub     c_t1, c_t0
                mov     g_lat, c_t1
                mov     g_del, #1
                jmp     #w_done
w_miss          mov     g_lat, c_window
                mov     g_del, #0
w_done          mov     g_pre, c_p2                     ' pre-flags: bit 0 p1, bit 1 p2, bit 2 ack
                shl     g_pre, #1
                or      g_pre, c_p1                     ' p2 << 1 | p1
                mov     c_tmp, c_ack
                shl     c_tmp, #2
                or      g_pre, c_tmp
                mov     g_tag, c_prog
                add     g_tag, c_tagbase
                ' record address = recbase + ((form * 3 + kind) * REPS + rep) * RECW * 4
                mov     c_idx, c_form
                shl     c_idx, #1
                add     c_idx, c_form                   ' form * 3
                add     c_idx, c_kind
                shl     c_idx, #3                       ' * REPS (8)
                add     c_idx, c_rep
                shl     c_idx, #4                       ' * RECW * 4 (16)
                add     c_idx, c_recbase
                setq    #RECW - 1
                wrlong  g_tag, c_idx                    ' the record, 4 longs, tag first
                add     c_kind, #1
                cmp     c_kind, #NKIND                  wz
        if_nz   jmp     #kind_lp
                add     c_form, #1
                cmp     c_form, #NPFORM                 wz
        if_nz   jmp     #form_lp
                add     c_rep, #1
                cmp     c_rep, #REPS                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #rep_lp
                wrlong  c_donev, ptra[MB_TDONE]
                cogid   c_tmp
                cogstop c_tmp

'--- cog data
c_window        long    WINDOW
c_ackbud        long    ACK_BUDGET
c_tagbase       long    TAG_BASE
c_donev         long    DONE_V
c_recbase       long    0
c_me            long    0
c_selfmask      long    0
c_rid           long    0
c_rep           long    0
c_form          long    0
c_kind          long    0
c_prog          long    0
c_tmp           long    0
c_idx           long    0
c_p1            long    0
c_p2            long    0
c_ack           long    0
c_t0            long    0
c_t1            long    0
c_dl            long    0
'--- the cell record, written as one 4-long block in this order (C_* order)
g_tag           long    0
g_del           long    0
g_lat           long    0
g_pre           long    0
target_end

